- 91 per cent of deaths were in British Columbia.
While the vast majority of British Columbians who died from illicit drug toxicity had a documented substance use issue, most deaths occurred outside the context of a treatment or harm-reduction centre.
“In 2017, 75 per cent of deaths occurred outside the context of a centre, and this is a trend that has been developing since 2013,” said Lapointe. “This data represents a need to work together to better understand these trends and develop innovative and collaborative solutions to address this public health crisis.”
